# Settings of the wrapper scripts in .gnomish/factory/, sourced by them as bash.
#
# The factory's own settings (factory.*) are NOT here: the factory reads them from its home —
# ~/.gnomish/projects/gnomish-factory/project.yaml for this project, ~/.gnomish/factory.yaml
# for the whole host (docs/adr/0011-operator-configuration-levels.md). The sandbox boundary
# (binding, image, egress allowlist, env passthrough) is read from project.yaml and nowhere
# else. Template beside this file: project.yaml.example.host.
#
# Reference:
#   docs/guides/operator-guide.md          — factory home, project registry, levels, secrets
#   docs/guides/operator-guide-serve.md    — factory.serve.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Wrapper and logging

# The name every clone of this repository is registered under
# (`gnomish project add gnomish-factory --dir=...`). Keys the project folder
# ~/.gnomish/projects/<name>/: settings, secrets, logs, serve state, worktrees.
GNOMISH_PROJECT_NAME=gnomish-factory

# Optional. The factory instance this clone runs as. Unset means the factory's default
# instance. Set a distinct one in gnomish.local.env when two clones of this repository run
# a daemon at the same time: the instance keys the log file and the serve state, and two
# daemons sharing one would interleave their narratives and overwrite each other's snapshot.
# GNOMISH_INSTANCE_NAME=

# Optional. The factory jar to launch; defaults to gnomish.jar beside the wrapper.
# GNOMISH_JAR=

# The Java launcher that runs the jar (Java 25).
GNOMISH_JAVA=java

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gnome rounds

# Subagents run one at a time in every gnome round: a parallel fan-out spends the shared
# Claude usage limit in minutes. Reaches the gnome only because project.yaml lists it under
# factory.sandbox.env-passthrough (template: project.yaml.example.host).
CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_CONCURRENT_SUBAGENTS=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# gnomish-up (daemon with its embedded dashboard + log follower in one terminal)

# Where the daemon writes the dashboard page (`serve --dashboard-out`). Inside the clone,
# git-ignored.
GNOMISH_DASHBOARD_DIR="$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/logs"

# Parallel task slots for `serve` when no --slots is passed.
GNOMISH_UP_SLOTS=1

# How long to wait for the daemon's first dashboard render before giving up on opening the
# browser (the daemon keeps running either way).
GNOMISH_UP_RENDER_WAIT_SECONDS=30
